d more flavor more texture more  nutrition without kind of ruffling the  feathers too much I'm just gonna saute  this rice cauliflower in oil with a  little pinch of salt until it's softened  and then I'm going to stir in the cooked  rice the white from the cauliflower the  white from the rice just gonna melt  together beautifully and look like a  really pleasing familiar food for your  kids this is ready to go and now we're  ready to plate my son likes his chana  masala with the rice my daughter likes  them super separate it's all good I'm  also gonna add a piece of butter naan to  this and garnish with cilantro which you  can totally omit if they don't like  green bits if all they end up eating is  the rice and the naan it's fine they got  some veggies they got a familiar food  and they got exposed to a new food I  love this dish it's packed with flavor  it's super quick it's super easy  let's try I like to tell my kids make a  boat with the naan and let's see what we  can tile into the boat gotta use all the  tricks mmm on point this was delicious  definitely a pallet adventure but if you  want to go back to something safer mega  kid-approved my  dish is exactly what you want next up  I'm making chicken kabobs which is a  really classic recipe in my family first  we're gonna add onion garlic and ginger  some fresh cilantro mint turmeric cumin  coriander and paprika salt to taste  about a teaspoon and then we're just  gonna blend this all up you just want it  to come together into kind of a spice  paste okay this looks good we're just  gonna fold the spice mixture into our  ground meat when I take my son to India  for the first time my mom made like a  hundred of these no joke and put them in  the freezer and just kept pulling them  out and serving them and my son kept  eating them and I was like this recipe  is a keeper these are SuperDuper  kid-approved but they're also amazing if  you're having a cocktail party and you  wanna have some finger food delicious  mi